[repo-allocation name=cx-repos
  [doc [#
THE REPO ALLOCATION — every tracked path in this tree, assigned to the
repository it moves to under the approved multi-repo shape (#1589, the owner
approved the shape 2026-09-21; the execution tracker is #1591). This file is
the allocation as DATA; scripts/repos_allocation_gate.cx is the check that
every tracked file lands in exactly one repo and that no rule here is dead.
It is what each extraction's history filter consumes, and it is the #1077
lesson — enumerate every artifact dimension before anything moves — made
executable.

Nothing here carries a `RULED:` id yet: the decision page superseding
cx_partition.md §5/§5.1 is item 5 on #1591. Until it lands this file states
the plan, and the gate keeps the plan total over the tree.

TWO KINDS OF ROW.
  [repo name= group= ring= ships= about=]
      one row per destination repository. `group` is the front-page group
      (core | platform | binding | ecosystem | dist), `ring` is 0, 1 or none,
      `ships` is how the repo reaches a user (binary | package | pypi | crate |
      go-module | v-module | editor | none | archived).
  [path prefix= repo=]  /  [path exact= repo=]
      one allocation rule. A tracked file belongs to the FIRST rule, in
      document order, whose `exact` equals the path or whose `prefix` is a
      leading substring of it. Specific rules are therefore written ABOVE
      general ones; the gate refuses a rule that matches no file, which is how
      a shadowed or stale rule is caught.

HOW TO READ A DECISION HERE. Where a module's repo is not the obvious one,
the rule carries a `why=`. The recurring reasons, once:
  - split by PRODUCT, not by dependency graph (owner, 2026-09-21);
  - the ring membership test (cx_partition.md §10): a module that imports
    nothing and opens no socket is Ring 1 and lives with the language —
    did, vc, authz, bus, the xsp frame codec, iowatch;
  - a shared codec stays in the language repo: saml/scim/oidc/soap/graphql/
    ws/email/http-client have callers outside the one product;
  - a module whose only consumer is one product moves to that product:
    ft → store, sasl → mail, diagram → tooling;
  - the store owns engine, streams (journal/live/audit) AND server, as
    Postgres does; the session module sits above it in identity;
  - `scripts/`, `tools/`, `docs*/`, `bench/`, `examples/`, `_gate_evidence/`
    and the root files are the build, release, site and evidence machinery of
    the whole — they go to `cx`, the distribution repo, and are re-homed per
    repo as each extraction lands (a repo takes its own gates with it).
#]]

  [; ── the destinations ─────────────────────────────────────────────── ]
  [repo name=cx group=dist ring=none ships=binary about='the front door: pins every repo, builds the four cx builds and libcx-core/libcx, holds the site, the release, the installer']
  [repo name=cx-core-data group=core ring=0 ships=binary about='the data format: reader, writer, canonical form, schema, codecs, libcx-core, the data-only cx']
  [repo name=cx-core-code group=core ring=1 ships=binary about='the language: evaluator, stdlib, LSP, libcx, the cli and embed builds']
  [repo name=cx-platform-net group=platform ring=none ships=binary about='sockets, TLS, the HTTP server, the XSP transport bindings, ftp, sftp, file_surface']
  [repo name=cx-platform-mail group=platform ring=none ships=binary about='SMTP and IMAP, server and client cores, sasl']
  [repo name=cx-platform-identity group=platform ring=none ships=binary about='sessions, the XSP-AUTH handshake, principal mint, did:web']
  [repo name=cx-platform-store group=platform ring=none ships=binary about='the storage engine, its substrates, journal/live/audit, ft, and the store server']
  [repo name=cx-platform-db group=platform ring=none ships=binary about='external database access: $sql-*, $redis-*, the drivers']
  [repo name=cx-platform-fabric group=platform ring=none ships=binary about='messaging and fabric-serve']
  [repo name=cx-platform-xap group=platform ring=none ships=binary about='the application host, compose, dist, schema, market, the reference deployments']
  [repo name=cx-platform-flow group=platform ring=none ships=package about='workflow; its CLI verbs stay in the binary']
  [repo name=cx-platform-connector group=platform ring=none ships=package about='the connector kit and sync']
  [repo name=cx-platform-sso group=platform ring=none ships=package about='enterprise sign-on, the interop lane']
  [repo name=cx-platform-ux group=platform ring=none ships=package about='the web and terminal surfaces']
  [repo name=cx-platform-agent group=platform ring=none ships=package about='tools, mcp, mcp-server, a2a, a2a-xap, llm, run, adjudicate']
  [repo name=cx-binding-python group=binding ring=none ships=pypi about='cxlib for Python']
  [repo name=cx-binding-go group=binding ring=none ships=go-module about='cxlib for Go']
  [repo name=cx-binding-rust group=binding ring=none ships=crate about='cxlib for Rust']
  [repo name=cx-binding-v group=binding ring=none ships=v-module about='the native reference binding']
  [repo name=cx-binding-typescript group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-java group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-kotlin group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-csharp group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-swift group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-ruby group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-registry group=ecosystem ring=none ships=none about='the package index: the store, publisher keys, the publish program']
  [repo name=cx-decisions group=ecosystem ring=none ships=none about='the ledger, the process specs, the standing rules, design texts']
  [repo name=cx-tooling group=ecosystem ring=none ships=editor about='vscode, neovim, tree-sitter, completions, syntax, the installer, diagram']

